{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310530,"nonce":"Mzhor5LckI3WMoMcIoomuox+hE4=","title":"Follow-up to the array_push fix: audited Array\u003cFloat\u003e.{push, unshift, insert} and Map\u003cK,Float\u003e.{set, get} for the same `Any`-shaped param ...","message":"- `build_array_unshift`: value param now `IrType::I64` (was `Any`).\n- runtime_mapping: `Array.unshift` uses `mir_wrapper, types: \u0026[PtrVoid, I64]`.\n- F64↔I64 bitcast at `build_call_direct` coercion preserves bits across the integer-typed slot.\n\nThe old mapping used `ptr_params: 0b100` which routed `Float` through\n`haxe_box_float_ptr` (→ heap-allocated DynamicValue). The runtime then\ncopied 8 bytes of DynamicValue header into the array slot. Wrong bytes,\nsilent corruption.\n\nFix: new `build_array_insert` MIR wrapper takes `(arr: Ptr\u003cVoid\u003e, pos: I32,\nvalue: I64)`, stack-allocates 8 bytes (`alloc(I64)`), stores the value, and\npasses the stack pointer as the runtime's `data: *const u8`. Runtime memcpys\n`elem_size` bytes from it. F64 callers get the F64→I64 bitcast at the call\nsite (the same fix as push).\n\nThe `Any`-shaped i64 path was the array side; the Map side uses\n`raw_value_params: 0b100` which makes the value param `U64`. The\n`maybe_box_for_extern_call` had only `Ptr → U64` covered. Added F64,\nF32, I32, I64 → U64 bitcast cases. Verified with `m.set(\"pi\", 3.14)`\nfollowed by inspecting the runtime: writes the correct f64 bit pattern\n(0x400921FB54442D1F for π, etc.).\n\n\nThe user's intuition that the U64 was \"an opaque pointer to a Dynamic\nBox\" pointed at the right structural issue. Instrumenting the dispatcher\nat [hir_to_mir.rs:12613](compiler/src/ir/hir_to_mir.rs#L12613) showed:\n\n```\nruntime=haxe_stringmap_get rt=Ptr(U8) rvt=Some(F64) eff=Ptr(U8)\n```\n\n- `result_type = Ptr(U8)` — the HIR types `Map.get` as `Null\u003cV\u003e` which\n  boxes to `Ptr(U8)`. The matcher's `IrType::F64` arm wasn't firing\n  because the visible type was `Ptr(U8)`, not `F64`.\n- `resolved_value_ty = Some(F64)` — the receiver's last type arg correctly\n  resolved V to F64.\n\nThe downstream `_ =\u003e` arm at line 12702 then cast U64 → I64 (preserving\nbits as integer), expecting downstream unboxing. But the runtime stores\nraw bits directly (no DynamicValue wrapper) — there's nothing to unbox.\n\nFix: a `result_is_opaque` predicate (Any | I64 | Ptr\u003cU8\u003e | Ptr\u003cVoid\u003e) plus\nan `effective_ty` reroute that picks `resolved_value_ty` for F64/F32 when\nthe visible result_type is opaque. The match then hits the existing F64\nbitcast arm.\n\n```rust\nlet result_is_opaque = match \u0026result_type {\n    IrType::Any | IrType::I64 =\u003e true,\n    IrType::Ptr(inner) =\u003e matches!(**inner, IrType::U8 | IrType::Void),\n    _ =\u003e false,\n};\nlet effective_ty = match resolved_value_ty.as_ref() {\n    Some(rty @ (IrType::F64 | IrType::F32)) if result_is_opaque =\u003e rty.clone(),\n    _ =\u003e result_type.clone(),\n};\nlet final_result = match \u0026effective_ty { ... };\n```\n\nVerified:\n- `Map\u003cString, Float\u003e.get` → 3.14, 2.718, 1.414 ✓\n- `Map\u003cInt, Float\u003e.get` → 3.14 ✓\n- `Map\u003cString, Int\u003e.get` → 42 (unchanged behavior) ✓\n- `Map\u003cString, Bool\u003e.get` → true ✓\n- `Map\u003cString, String\u003e.get` with explicit `var v:String` → \"hello\" ✓\n  (string-concat form still shows pointer-as-int, a pre-existing\n  behaviour unrelated to the F64 fix)\n\n\n- `array_set` via `arr[i] = v` for f64 — earlier tests showed it works for\n  small arrays, but the underlying path (`haxe_array_set` with raw bytes)\n  may rely on the same broken boxing for f64 in other shapes. Re-verify\n  with cross-context Array\u003cFloat\u003e and mixed-type arrays.\n- `array_splice` insert mode with f64 — likely the same boxing path as\n  the old `array_insert`.\n- `Map.exists` / `Map.remove` are read-only and shouldn't be affected, but\n  worth a smoke check.\n- WeakMap, ObjectMap with Float values — same `raw_value_params: 0b100`\n  shape as StringMap; set side is fixed via the same `maybe_box_for_extern_call`\n  change, get side has the same outstanding bug.\n\n\n- [[bugs-array-float-push-any-param]] — the Phase 1 fix; this is the (a) sweep follow-up.\n- [[bugs-gguf-q6k-and-f32-load]] — the original session that surfaced the precision class of bugs.\n- [[bugs-null-int-cross-file-assign]] — same shape (coercion gap at call boundary) for Int. Still pending.\n- [[bugs-test-exception-flake]] — unrelated pre-existing ~30% SIGTRAP flake on test_exception.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_array_map_float_audit` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}